# 🤓: BFO_0000016 = Disposition — the disposition to Continue OR Break is a
# genuine BFO disposition: it inheres in a process and is realized by the gate.

## Problem

# b00t gates (bouncer, hive-guards, delegation macro checks) all implement
# a binary Continue/Break decision but lack a TYPED shared abstraction:

# 1. Guards return `GuardAction::Allow | Warn | Block` (ad-hoc strings)
# 2. Bouncer uses ad-hoc `Result<()>` for pass/fail
# 3. Delegation macros expand unconditionally (no gate type)
# 4. No ontological representation → can't query "which processes have a ControlFlow gate?"

# Rust's `std::ops::ControlFlow<B, C>` is the canonical correct type for this:
# - `Continue(C)` = proceed with value C
# - `Break(B)` = halt with value B

# b00t needs to ADOPT this type throughout and REPRESENT it in the ontology.

## Finished State

### Rust: Gate trait using ControlFlow

# ```rust
# use std::ops::ControlFlow;

# /// Universal gate trait used by bouncer, guards, and delegation macros.
# pub trait Gate<B, C> {
#     fn evaluate(&self, ctx: &GateContext) -> ControlFlow<B, C>;
# }

# /// Standard gate types (parameterized):
# /// Guard gate: ControlFlow<BlockReason, Command>
# /// Bouncer gate: ControlFlow<DenialAuditRecord, ValidatedInput>
# /// Delegation macro: ControlFlow<MacroError, ExpandedCommand>
# ```

### Ontological Mapping (OWL2 / BFO)

# | Rust type | BFO class | SysMLv2 stereotype | OWL2 class |
# |---|---|---|---|
# | `ControlFlow<B,C>` | BFO_0000016 (Disposition) | «ConstraintBlock» | b00t:ControlFlowGate |
# | `Continue(C)` | BFO_0000015 (Process) | «FlowPort» outgoing | b00t:ContinueFlow |
# | `Break(B)` | BFO_0000023 (Role) | «FlowPort» blocked | b00t:BreakFlow |

### CLIF Axioms (authored in [b00t.clif], transpile to OWL2)

# ```
# Every ControlFlow gate is exactly one of Continue or Break (disjoint union)
# (forall (x) (if (ControlFlowGate x) (or (ContinueFlow x) (BreakFlow x))))
# (forall (x) (not (and (ContinueFlow x) (BreakFlow x))))

# A Guard that issues Block IS a BreakFlow
# (forall (x) (if (and (Guard x) (issues-block x)) (BreakFlow x)))
# ```

### Higher-Order Gate Patterns (datum sub-stereotypes)

# | Pattern | b00t.type | ControlFlow signature |
# |---|---|---|
# | Bouncer | `pattern__gate__bouncer` | `ControlFlow<DenialRecord, ValidatedInput>` |
# | Guard | `pattern__gate__guard` | `ControlFlow<BlockReason, Command>` |
# | Handoff | `pattern__gate__handoff` | `ControlFlow<HandoffError, AgentContext>` |
# | Rate Limiter | `pattern__gate__ratelimit` | `ControlFlow<QuotaExceeded, TokenBudget>` |
# | OKR Gate | `pattern__gate__okr` | `ControlFlow<KrFail, KrPass>` |

# All inherit from `pattern__gate` which maps to `ControlFlow<B,C>` abstract type.

### b00t hive guard alignment

# Current: `GuardAction::Allow | Warn | Block`
# Target:  `ControlFlow<GuardBlock, GuardAllow>`

# ```rust
# pub struct GuardAllow { pub command: String, pub redirect: Option<String> }
# pub struct GuardBlock { pub reason: String, pub message: String }
# pub type GuardFlow = ControlFlow<GuardBlock, GuardAllow>;
# ```

# The `repeat_threshold` field becomes a rate-limit sub-gate:
# `ControlFlow<ThresholdExceeded, GuardAllow>`.

### Handoff Pattern (explicit typed)

# ```rust
# pub struct HandoffContext {
#     pub from_agent: String,
#     pub to_agent: String,
#     pub task_id: String,
#     pub artifacts: Vec<Artifact>,
#     pub blockers: Vec<String>,
# }

# pub enum HandoffGate {
#     Continue(HandoffContext),  // artifacts verified, proceed
#     Break(HandoffError),       // missing artifact / wrong tier
# }
# ```

# Represented in datum: `b00t.type = "pattern__gate__handoff"`.

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `Gate<B,C>` trait in `b00t-bouncer/src/lib.rs` using `std::ops::ControlFlow`
# - [ ] `GuardFlow = ControlFlow<GuardBlock, GuardAllow>` in `b00t-cli/src/hive.rs`
# - [ ] `b00t.clif` CLIF axioms added to OWL2 ontology (PRD-ARCH-006)
# - [ ] `pattern__gate` and sub-stereotypes queryable via `b00t datum filter --types=pattern__gate`
# - [ ] Handoff pattern datum: `HANDOFF-PATTERN.pattern__gate.tomllmd`
# - [ ] Bouncer datum updated: `[b00t.type] = "pattern__gate__bouncer"`
# - [ ] OWL2 reasoning: query "which datums have ControlFlow gates?" via `b00t datums graph`

